        "original_id": "1f14829b-bd4d-50ee-a773-4532d1b805a4",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Chrysler F platform, Chrysler K platform, Plymouth Fury\n- Companies: Chrysler, Plymouth\n- Concepts: compact-sized cars, non-American designs\n\nFacts:\n- The Plymouth Fury was an automobile model produced by Plymouth from 1955 to 1989.\n- The Chrysler F platform was effectively replaced by the Chrysler K platform.\n- The Chrysler K platform was offered in standard and stretch sizes.\n- The Chrysler K platform retained two bench seats, a column shifter, and room for six.\n- Many other compact-sized cars modeled after non-American designs did not retain two bench seats, a column shifter, and room for six.\n- The Chrysler K platform was very successful.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
